{"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note","doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note\/Beam-swift.struct"]]},"metadata":{"roleHeading":"API Collection","role":"collectionGroup","title":"Equatable Implementations","modules":[{"name":"IvorMXL"}]},"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note\/Beam-swift.struct\/!=(_:_:)"],"generated":true,"anchor":"Operators","title":"Operators"}],"kind":"article","variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/note\/beam-swift.struct\/equatable-implementations"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"minor":3,"patch":0},"identifier":{"interfaceLanguage":"swift","url":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note\/Beam-swift.struct\/Equatable-Implementations"},"references":{"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL":{"type":"topic","title":"IvorMXL","kind":"symbol","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"A MusicXML parser, normalizer, validator, and formatter."}],"role":"collection","url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/Note/Beam-swift.struct/!=(_:_:)":{"type":"topic","abstract":[],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/note\/beam-swift.struct\/!=(_:_:)","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"static"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"func"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"!="},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"text","text":"("},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":", "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Self"},{"kind":"text","text":") -> "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Bool","preciseIdentifier":"s:Sb"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"!=(_:_:)","identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note\/Beam-swift.struct\/!=(_:_:)","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The metronome type represents metronome marks and other metric relationships. The beat-unit group and per-"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"minute element specify regular metronome marks. The metronome-note and metronome-relation elements allow for"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the specification of metric modulations and other metric relationships, such as swing tempo marks where two"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"eighths are equated to a quarter note \/ eighth note triplet. Tied notes can be represented in both types of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"metronome marks by using the beat-unit-tied and metronome-tied elements. The parentheses attribute indicates"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"whether or not to put the metronome mark in parentheses; its value is no if not specified. The print-object"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"attribute is set to no in cases where the metronome element represents a relationship or range that is not"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"displayed in the music notation."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLMetronome","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"MXLMetronome"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/Note/Beam-swift.struct":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The metronome-beam type works like the beam type in defining metric relationships, but does not include all"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the attributes available in the beam type."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/note\/beam-swift.struct","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Beam"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLMetronome.Note.Beam","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Beam"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note\/Beam-swift.struct","role":"symbol"},"doc://IvorMXL/documentation/IvorMXL/MXLMetronome/Note":{"type":"topic","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The metronome-note type defines the appearance of a note within a metric relationship mark."}],"url":"\/documentation\/ivormxl\/mxlmetronome\/note","fragments":[{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"Note"}],"kind":"symbol","title":"MXLMetronome.Note","navigatorTitle":[{"kind":"identifier","text":"Note"}],"identifier":"doc:\/\/IvorMXL\/documentation\/IvorMXL\/MXLMetronome\/Note","role":"symbol"}}}